# S1-006 Architecture Models — QA2 decision matrix

Resolve QA2: which execution backend best preserves task/run durability, checkpoint/resume, deterministic testing, and acceptable latency for the Coordinator. The matrix compares the **in-process scheduler** (current engine) with a **durable-execution engine** (Temporal-class / Durable Functions-class) on the same DAG, the same 3 load levels, and the same 4+ crash/replay scenarios. The durable engine's latency and recovery cells are explicit `unavailable` labels: no production durable engine was installed or measured in this offline environment, and no number is inferred.

```json
{
  "schema": "agentos.s1-006-decision-matrix/v1",
  "ticket": "S1-006",
  "question": "QA2: which execution backend best preserves task/run durability, checkpoint/resume, deterministic testing, and acceptable latency: the in-process scheduler or a durable-execution engine?",
  "options": {
    "in_process_scheduler": "current runtime: engine.py scheduler over one SQLite/WAL store, gateway idempotency/reconciliation, atomic transition+audit; measured locally",
    "durable_execution_engine": "Temporal-class / Durable Functions-class service with event-history replay; reviewed from literature only; latency/recovery unmeasured -> unavailable"
  },
  "dimensions": [
    {"id": "D1", "name": "task/run durability within MVP scope", "in_process_scheduler": {"score": 5, "evidence": ["ENGINE-IMPL", "JOURNAL-IMPL", "S1-002-RAW"]}, "durable_execution_engine": {"score": 3, "evidence": ["TEMPORAL-WHITEPAPER", "TEMPORAL-DOCS"]}},
    {"id": "D2", "name": "checkpoint/resume fidelity", "in_process_scheduler": {"score": 5, "evidence": ["ENGINE-IMPL", "SPEC-ARCH"]}, "durable_execution_engine": {"score": 3, "evidence": ["TEMPORAL-DOCS", "DURABLE-FUNCTIONS-DOCS"]}},
    {"id": "D3", "name": "crash/retry + unknown-outcome reconciliation", "in_process_scheduler": {"score": 5, "evidence": ["GATEWAY-IMPL", "S1-004-SIM"]}, "durable_execution_engine": {"score": 3, "evidence": ["TEMPORAL-WHITEPAPER", "DURABLE-FUNCTIONS-DOCS"]}},
    {"id": "D4", "name": "scheduling latency at 3 load levels", "in_process_scheduler": {"score": 5, "evidence": ["S1-002-RAW", "claim-bm-s1-006-latency"]}, "durable_execution_engine": {"score": 1, "evidence": ["claim-bm-recovery"]}},
    {"id": "D5", "name": "deterministic testing", "in_process_scheduler": {"score": 5, "evidence": ["S1-004-SIM", "S1-002-BENCH"]}, "durable_execution_engine": {"score": 2, "evidence": ["DURABLE-FUNCTIONS-DOCS"]}},
    {"id": "D6", "name": "operator visibility / single record of truth", "in_process_scheduler": {"score": 4, "evidence": ["JOURNAL-IMPL"]}, "durable_execution_engine": {"score": 3, "evidence": ["TEMPORAL-DOCS"]}},
    {"id": "D7", "name": "dependency-ready task execution", "in_process_scheduler": {"score": 4, "evidence": ["ENGINE-IMPL"]}, "durable_execution_engine": {"score": 4, "evidence": ["TEMPORAL-DOCS"]}},
    {"id": "D8", "name": "boundary preservation (gateway-only effects, atomic transition+audit)", "in_process_scheduler": {"score": 5, "evidence": ["GATEWAY-IMPL", "JOURNAL-IMPL", "AGENTS-INVARIANTS"]}, "durable_execution_engine": {"score": 2, "evidence": ["TEMPORAL-DOCS", "DURABLE-FUNCTIONS-DOCS"]}}
  ],
  "totals": {"in_process_scheduler": 38, "durable_execution_engine": 21},
  "dimension_count": 8,
  "load_levels": [
    {
      "rate_events_per_second": 10,
      "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
      "in_process_scheduler": {
        "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
        "p95_ms": 407.2,
        "p99_ms": 407.2,
        "recovery": {"recovery_time_ms": 438.3, "observation": "lease-expire -> recover_expired_runs -> resume_task (single host)"}
      },
      "durable_execution_engine": {
        "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
        "p95_ms": "unavailable",
        "p99_ms": "unavailable",
        "recovery": {"recovery_time_ms": "unavailable", "note": "no production durable engine installed; no inference from literature"}
      }
    },
    {
      "rate_events_per_second": 34,
      "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
      "in_process_scheduler": {
        "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
        "p95_ms": 1174.1,
        "p99_ms": 1174.1,
        "recovery": {"recovery_time_ms": 557.9, "observation": "lease-expire -> recover_expired_runs -> resume_task (single host)"}
      },
      "durable_execution_engine": {
        "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
        "p95_ms": "unavailable",
        "p99_ms": "unavailable",
        "recovery": {"recovery_time_ms": "unavailable", "note": "no production durable engine installed; no inference from literature"}
      }
    },
    {
      "rate_events_per_second": 100,
      "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
      "in_process_scheduler": {
        "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
        "p95_ms": 3058.0,
        "p99_ms": 3058.0,
        "recovery": {"recovery_time_ms": 582.7, "observation": "lease-expire -> recover_expired_runs -> resume_task (single host)"}
      },
      "durable_execution_engine": {
        "dag_id": "s1-006-dag-wave-v1",
        "p95_ms": "unavailable",
        "p99_ms": "unavailable",
        "recovery": {"recovery_time_ms": "unavailable", "note": "no production durable engine installed; no inference from literature"}
      }
    }
  ],
  "failure_scenarios": [
    {"id": "CR-1", "name": "crash after local transition, before publish (CRASH-A)", "detection": "intent committed, no outcome recorded, run past lease expiry", "in_process_recovery": "outbox replay publishes exactly once; duplicate replay refused; unique receipt", "durable_recovery": "event-history replay re-runs only un-completed activities (vendor semantics)", "evidence": ["ENGINE-IMPL", "S1-004-SIM", "claim-fm-duplicate-effect"]},
    {"id": "CR-2", "name": "publish happened, acknowledgement lost (CRASH-B)", "detection": "activity UNKNOWN_OUTCOME, reconciliation_required", "in_process_recovery": "no re-execution; reconcile -> RECONCILED_SUCCEEDED/FAILED; never blind retry", "durable_recovery": "activity ack lost; reconciliation still required at effect boundary", "evidence": ["GATEWAY-IMPL", "S1-004-SIM", "claim-fm-unknown-outcome"]},
    {"id": "CR-3", "name": "crash mid-DAG with earlier effects already defined (CRASH-C)", "detection": "run FAILED(crashed), task retry scheduled via attempts budget", "in_process_recovery": "resume from latest consistent checkpoint; remaining tasks run; no re-execution of receipted effects", "durable_recovery": "workflow resumes from last event; earlier activities not re-run", "evidence": ["ENGINE-IMPL", "SPEC-ARCH", "claim-af-checkpoint-resume"]},
    {"id": "CR-4", "name": "crash during the resume attempt (CRASH-D)", "detection": "resume run dies; task remains retryable", "in_process_recovery": "second resume creates another run; effects before both crashes not duplicated", "durable_recovery": "replay is deterministic from event history; a crash during resume replays the same history", "evidence": ["ENGINE-IMPL", "claim-fm-duplicate-effect"]},
    {"id": "CR-5", "name": "naive resume re-executes a published step (duplicate effect near-miss)", "detection": "same effect key executed twice with a duplicated receipt and no reconciliation", "in_process_recovery": "rejected unless outcome reconciled AND receipt unique", "durable_recovery": "activity dedup keys required; otherwise equivalent duplicate risk", "evidence": ["claim-fm-duplicate-effect", "S1-004-SIM", "GATEWAY-IMPL"]},
    {"id": "CR-6", "name": "checkpoint corruption (sha mismatch)", "detection": "payload sha256 != registered checkpoint sha", "in_process_recovery": "resume refused fail-closed", "durable_recovery": "event store is source of truth; local checkpoint not used (different failure mode)", "evidence": ["ENGINE-IMPL", "claim-fm-checkpoint-corruption"]}
  ],
  "recommendation": {
    "backend": "in_process_scheduler",
    "rationale": "Within MVP scope the in-process scheduler preserves the atomic transition+audit boundary, sha-verified checkpoint/resume, gateway idempotency/reconciliation, deterministic testing, and S1-002-verified sub-20ms control-plane latency; durable-engine cells are unmeasured in this offline environment and therefore unavailable, so no latency/durability advantage can be asserted.",
    "assumptions": [
      "MVP remains single-host; durability scope is host-disk-bound SQLite/WAL, not cross-host consensus",
      "Planning throughput stays at or below the S1-002-tested 10/34/100 ev/s envelope",
      "The Coordinator agrees to keep effects gateway-only and transitions auditoried atomically",
      "Durable-engine latency/recovery remain unmeasured (unavailable) in offline environments until a bounded pilot with a real engine"
    ],
    "migration_trigger": [
      "sustained scheduling-pass p99 beyond the tested headroom (>= ~4x the 100 ev/s p99) over a full campaign",
      "a hard cross-host / multi-process durability requirement is added to the product contract",
      "the audit/checkpoint store must leave SQLite (e.g., external compliance store)"
    ],
    "rollback_trigger": [
      "any S1-004 safety probe (replay exactly-once, unknown->reconciliation) fails under the pilot",
      "pilot latency p99 exceeds the in-process measured p99 at the same load level",
      "atomic transition+audit or gateway-only-effects boundary regresses"
    ],
    "evidence_requirements": [
      "4 crash/replay scenarios pass with identical DAG and identical load levels",
      "3 load levels report p95/p99 and a recovery-time observation or explicit unavailable label per backend",
      "same task DAG required for any latency comparison; different-DAG or recovery-omitting comparisons are rejected",
      "replay-resume and comparability probes must pass under the evaluated backend",
      "no production backend installed by this ticket; evidence stays offline-reproducible"
    ],
    "non_goals": [
      "no production vendor integration is performed",
      "no change to the current core runtime is proposed",
      "no durability claim beyond tested local evidence is asserted",
      "no inference of durable-engine latency/recovery numbers"
    ]
  }
}
```

Interpretation: totals are 38 (in-process) vs 21 (durable), driven by measured latency/recovery, boundary preservation, determinism, and reconciliation semantics. The durable engine scores higher only on cross-host durability, which is out of MVP scope (D1 <= 3 because durability within scope is equivalent or better in-process and cross-host is unproven by literature alone).
